  "raw_text": "Step 1: The formula for the projection of vector $\\mathbf{a}$ onto vector $\\mathbf{b}$ is given by\n\\[\n\\text{proj}_{\\mathbf{b}} \\mathbf{a} = \\frac{\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}}{\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}} \\mathbf{b}.\n\\]\nStep 2: Given vectors are $\\mathbf{a} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ y \\\\ -5 \\end{pmatrix}$ and $\\mathbf{b} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}$, and the projection is $\\frac{5}{6} \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}$.\nStep 3: Calculate $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}$:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = 2(1) + y(-2) + (-5)(1) = 2 - 2y - 5 = -3 - 2y.\n\\]\nStep 4: Calculate $\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}$:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = 1^2 + (-2)^2 + 1^2 = 1 + 4 + 1 = 6.\n\\]\nStep 5: Substitute into the projection formula:\n\\[\n\\frac{-3 - 2y}{6} \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix} = \\frac{5}{6} \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\nStep 6: Equate the scalar multiples:\n\\[\n\\frac{-3 - 2y}{6} = \\frac{5}{6}.\n\\]\nStep 7: Solve for $y$:\n\\[\n-3 - 2y = 5 \\implies -2y = 8 \\implies y = -4.\n\\]\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{-4}<|im_end|>",
